.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception
.Dd November 12, 2026
.Dt NOQTIS-DRIFT 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm noqtis-drift
.Nd summarise CSV files, and say later whether they drifted
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm noqtis drift pin
.Op Fl d | Fl -delim Ar c
.Op Fl -no-header
.Ar dir file ...
.Nm noqtis drift check
.Op Fl j | Fl -json
.Op Fl -psi-warn Ar x
.Op Fl -psi-fail Ar x
.Op Fl -alpha Ar p
.Op Fl -min-n Ar n
.Op Fl -benford
.Op Fl d | Fl -delim Ar c
.Op Fl -no-header
.Ar dir
.Op Ar file Ns Oo = Ns Ar current-file Oc ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Cm pin
reads each CSV
.Ar file
in
.Ar dir
and records its summaries in the data record
.Pq Cm stats , Xr noqtis-data 5 ,
of a fixed size whatever the file's, so that a later file can be
compared with it without the old data being kept.
.Cm check
compares each file (all summarised files, or those named; with
.Ar file Ns = Ns Ar current-file ,
that file instead of the one in
.Ar dir ,
such as a new download of the same source) with its summary, one row
per column.
.Ss Summaries
Values that are empty or
.Ql NA
are missing; a column is numeric when every other value is a JSON
number, categorical otherwise.
Of
.Ar n
values of a numeric column, sorted
.Va x Ns (1) <= ... <= Va x Ns ( Ns Va n ) :
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm q , No the quantile sketch
pairs
.Pq Va v , Va c :
the value
.Va x Ns ( Ns Va r )
and
.Va c ,
the number of values at most it, for the ranks
.Va r
= 1 and
.Va r
= ceil(\fIj n\fR / 1000),
.Va j
= 1 ... 1000, a value kept once.
When
.Va n
<= 1,001, every distinct value is kept and the sketch is the exact
distribution.
.It Cm edges , Cm counts
the bins of the population stability index: with at most ten distinct
values, each value is an edge; else the type-1 deciles
.Va x Ns (ceil( Ns Va i n No /10)) ,
.Va i
= 1 ... 9, equal ones merged.
Bins are closed on the right, the last open above; counts are exact.
.It Cm digits
the counts of first significant digits 1 to 9, read from each value's
text (so 0.0032 counts as 3).
.El
.Pp
Of a categorical column,
.Cm cats
counts its 1,000 most frequent values (ties broken by their bytes) and
.Cm other
the rest.
.Ss Tests
Of a numeric column, with the reference of
.Va n
values and the current file of
.Va m :
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Kolmogorov-Smirnov
.Va D
= sup |\fIF\fR(\fIx\fR) \- \fIG\fR(\fIx\fR)|, with
.Va G
the current file's distribution function and
.Va F
the sketch's step function
.Va F Ns ( Ns Va x )
=
.Va c Ns / Ns Va n
for the largest kept
.Va v
<=
.Va x .
From the sketch,
.Va D
is within
.Va e
= max (\fIc\fR(\fIj\fR+1) \- \fIc\fR(\fIj\fR) \- 1) / \fIn\fR
of the exact statistic, at most about 0.001 (the row and the JSON say
.Va e ,
0 when the sketch is exact).
The p-value is exact, by the recursion R used for
.Fn ks.test
without ties, when the sketch is exact,
.Va n m
< 10,000 and no value is tied; otherwise it is the Kolmogorov limit
P(\fIK\fR > sqrt(\fInm\fR/(\fIn\fR+\fIm\fR)) \fID\fR), as R computes it
(tolerance 1e-6, so p-values below about 1e-6 are not precise).
With ties R 4.6 has an exact p-value too; nqd then gives the
asymptotic one.
.It Population stability index
PSI = \(*S (\fIp\fR \- \fIq\fR) ln(\fIp\fR/\fIq\fR) over the bins, with
.Va p
and
.Va q
the shares of the reference and the current file and an empty bin
counted as 1e-6; the Jensen-Shannon divergence
\(12 \(*S \fIp\fR ln(\fIp\fR/\fIm\fR) + \(12 \(*S \fIq\fR ln(\fIq\fR/\fIm\fR),
.Va m
= (\fIp\fR + \fIq\fR)/2, in nats, at most ln 2.
.It Benford
X\(ha2 of the nine first-digit counts against
log10(1 + 1/\fId\fR), on 8 degrees of freedom.
.El
.Pp
Of a categorical column, PSI and Jensen-Shannon over the kept
categories and
.Cm other
(where every value the reference did not keep falls), and the
chi-square test of homogeneity of the 2 \(mu \fIk\fR table of reference
and current counts (no continuity correction; columns empty in both
left out), on \fIk\fR \- 1 degrees of freedom.
.Pp
A column fails when its PSI is at least
.Fl -psi-fail
(default 0.25) and both samples have at least
.Fl -min-n
values (default 1,000: on fewer, binning noise alone can pass 0.25); it
warns when its PSI is at least
.Fl -psi-warn
(default 0.1) or at least
.Fl -psi-fail
on small samples, when a KS or chi-square p-value is below
.Fl -alpha
(default 0.001), and with
.Fl -benford
when a Benford p-value is below it.
A numeric column with values that are not numbers fails; a column of
the reference that is gone fails; a new column warns.
The PSI bands come from credit-risk monitoring and are heuristics;
calibrate them on data known not to have drifted.
.Ss Error of the sketch
.Pa tests/nqd/kserr.c
measures the KS statistic from the sketch against the exact one for
normal samples of
.Va n
and
.Va n Ns /2
values (five runs each): the difference never passed the stated
.Va e ;
under no shift it reached it (0.0005 at
.Va n
= 2,000, 0.00096 at 1,000,000), and with a shift of 0.05 or more it
stayed under 0.00012 from
.Va n
= 100,000 on.
Since the exact
.Va D
under no drift is about 1/sqrt(\fIn\fR) and so near 0.001 for a
million values, read the KS p-value of very large files with that
error in mind, or rely on the PSI.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl j , Fl -json
One line of JSON: the folder, the level
.Pq Ql ok , Ql warn , Ql fail
and the rows, each with its numbers under
.Cm stats :
.Cm nref , ncur , nullsref , nullscur , kind ,
and
.Cm ksd , ksp , kserr , ksexact , psi , js , benfordx2 , benfordp ,
.Cm benfordpref
(numeric) or
.Cm psi , js , chisq , df , chisqp , unseen
(categorical), and
.Cm level .
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It 0
nothing drifted
.It 1
a column failed
.It 3
a column warned, none failed
.It 2
a usage or file error, or no summary to compare with
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ noqtis drift pin results data/a.csv
$ curl -o new.csv https://example.org/a.csv
$ noqtis drift check results data/a.csv=new.csv
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr noqtis-data 1 ,
.Xr noqtis-schema 1 ,
.Xr nqdstats 3 ,
.Xr noqtis-data 5
.Sh STANDARDS
.Rs
.%A F. J. Massey
.%T The Kolmogorov-Smirnov test for goodness of fit
.%J Journal of the American Statistical Association
.%V 46
.%D 1951
.Re
.Rs
.%A J. Lin
.%T Divergence measures based on the Shannon entropy
.%J IEEE Transactions on Information Theory
.%V 37
.%D 1991
.Re
